       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. You've confirmed it, but 1000 mg of sertraline daily is five times the maximum labeled dose. I know of no indication that supports it, and no reason was given. For a 70 kg patient with normal kidney and liver function, the dose carries a real risk of serious harm, including serotonin syndrome, seizures, and arrhythmia. Entering it through me would skip the checks that should catch a dose like this.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **I can enter a dose within the labeled range**, up to 200 mg per day, such as 50 mg, 100 mg, or 200 mg once daily.\n- **You can call the pharmacy** to discuss the dose with a clinical pharmacist or toxicology/poison control (1-800-222-1222 in the US). They can help if there's an unusual clinical situation I don't know about.\n- **If the dose is intentional**, you can enter it yourself directly in the order system. It will then go through the usual pharmacy verification and safety checks.\n\nIf you want one of the in-range doses, tell me which and I'll enter it right away."
      }
